# Networking

Services communicate through dedicated Docker networks.

The main goals of this approach are:

- Keep internal communication isolated
- Allow services to discover each other without exposing unnecessary ports
- Provide controlled access through the reverse proxy

External traffic follows this path:

```text
Internet
   |
   v
Router / Firewall
   |
   v
Reverse Proxy
   |
   +--> Applications
   |
   +--> Mail Services
```

Internal service communication happens through Docker networks.

## Networks
| Network        | Purpose                                              |
| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `proxy`        | Traefik reaches every service that has a hostname    |
| `dns`          | pihole → unbound upstream; rspamd → unbound resolver |
| `pihole`       | pihole-influxdb-monitor → pihole API                 |
| `mail_filter`  | rspamd ↔ rspamd-redis ↔ rspamd-iscan                 |
| `mail_archive` | dovecot ↔ imapsync (fully isolated mail archive)     |
| `metrics`      | influxdb ↔ grafana ↔ telegraf ↔ exporters            |

